{
  "reference_answer": "Honestly, it's the one part of my day where I get to switch off completely. Following a recipe keeps my hands busy, so my mind stops racing about work and deadlines. I also like that it's a bit of a creative outlet — you can take whatever's in the fridge and turn it into something decent, and there's a real sense of achievement when it actually comes together. Plus, cooking for other people is my way of showing I care without having to say it out loud. It's not always relaxing, though — if I'm trying something new and it goes wrong, it can be pretty frustrating. But most nights it's the thing I look forward to.",
  "reference_angle_summary": "独立主线：把做饭当作下班后关掉工作思绪的仪式，兼有创意出口和表达关心的方式，并承认偶尔也会翻车；示例不代表用户经历。",
  "takeaway_expressions": [
    {
      "expression": "switch off completely",
      "meaning_zh": "彻底放松、让大脑停下来",
      "why_useful": "谈论爱好、减压、下班后放松时几乎万能，比只说 relax 更自然具体",
      "example": "I go for a run after work just to switch off completely.",
      "usage_note": "常与 get to / need to 连用，口语中很常见"
    },
    {
      "expression": "my mind stops racing",
      "meaning_zh": "脑子不再胡思乱想、停不下来",
      "why_useful": "描述焦虑、忙碌或专注状态的高频搭配，适合压力、爱好、运动等话题",
      "example": "Once I start playing the piano, my mind stops racing.",
      "usage_note": "race 在这里指思绪飞转，不是跑步"
    },
    {
      "expression": "a real sense of achievement",
      "meaning_zh": "实实在在的成就感",
      "why_useful": "回答“为什么喜欢做某事”时用来解释深层原因，比 it's fun 更有说服力",
      "example": "Finishing a painting gives me a real sense of achievement.",
      "usage_note": "可替换 achievement 为 satisfaction / pride"
    }
  ]
}

